  "ties_note": "randomized NP test; exact at the atom. c is the smallest H0 value with P0(L > c) \u2264 \u03b1. \u03b3 = (\u03b1\u00b7n0 \u2212 #{L0 > c}) / #{L0 == c}, clipped to [0, 1]. Power = P1(L > c) + \u03b3\u00b7P1(L == c). A +inf ratio always rejects.",
  "power_se_formula": "Conditional on the H0 pair (c, gamma), each H1 replicate has weight W = 1{L = +inf or L > c} + gamma\u00b71{L finite and L = c}. power = mean(W). SE = sqrt((mean(W^2) - power^2) / n1). This is the multinomial delta-method SE of the randomized estimator. W is only 0, gamma, or 1, so the moments are the three class counts, not a running sum: a constant weight then has SE 0. When gamma is 0 or 1, W is Bernoulli and SE equals the binomial SE sqrt(p(1-p)/n1).",
